comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T10:04:53.215Z","harness:opencode","Candidate edge for the changelog-safe batch (found 2026-07-26): pm-cu1i (closed, token-budget ratchet) -> related pm-a22j (closed, token baseline). The ratchet's body states it turns the a22j one-time baseline into a permanent CI ratchet; the edge is semantically true but touches two terminal items, so it belongs to this wave, not an ad-hoc pass."
  "2026-08-13T08:46:47.325Z","harness:claude-code","Batch executed for three of four codes, changelog effect measured first rather than assumed.\n\nBefore: 11 findings; nodes 2458 (missing_nodes 3); edges 12116; tracker-context-quality verdict pass.\n\nExecuted:\n- legacy_duplicate_edge 8 -> 0. Collapsed 8 reciprocal child rows onto the canonical parent edge each child already stored: pm-7t04 (5 rows: 0nia, 1265, 8rjn, b8rf, g2nd) and pm-v7dj (3 rows: aqat, jauk, ze5g). Lossless, because parent and child are declared inverses and every child stores the parent spelling.\n- missing_reference_terminal 3 -> 0. Removed pm-1p2u's related row to the non-existent pm-0wm0, and cleared two legacy free-text blocked_by scalars that were never item ids (pm-lty 'backlog-sequencing', pm-zdec 'design-review').\n- legacy_no_blocker_sentinel 98 -> 0. Cleared the retired no-active-blocker scalar on all 98 holders; blocker state now derives from real edges only.\n\nAfter: 8 findings, all legacy_ordering_cycle; nodes 2455; edges 12105.\n\nChangelog effect, measured not assumed: regeneration diff was 15 lines, all intra-section reordering of the four touched closed items within their own already-published release sections. No item entered [Unreleased]; no section gained or lost an item. All 98 sentinel holders and all 4 touched items carry a release value, which is the field the generator buckets by. Filed as pm-71v4l9: the closed_at rule this item's body relies on over-counts the risky population by 4.4x (1475 vs the real 337).\n\nFourth code not executed, and it is not a scheduling choice: the root cause of all 8 cycles is now known (26 holders storing a scalar blocked_by X together with a contradicting structured row X,blocks; full list on pm-xvt7ps), the repair is mechanical, and removing those 26 rows takes edges to 12079 against graph-edges-floor 12103 at block enforcement. Recorded blocked_by pm-mfvsng."
  "2026-08-13T09:00:19.489Z","harness:claude-code","CI hardening attempted and blocked, recorded so the earned state is not mistaken for an enforced one.\n\nThe three ceilings this batch drove to zero are still declared at their pre-batch values: graph-finding-legacy-duplicate-edge-ceiling 8, graph-finding-legacy-no-blocker-sentinel-ceiling 98, graph-finding-missing-reference-terminal-ceiling 3. Tightening them to 0 is what converts this batch from a one-off cleanup into a regression gate, and it is the whole reason the batch is worth doing.\n\nEvery attempt fails: 'Workspace history state for assurance.json changed outside the audited mutation path.' The refusal is correct and predates this session — the committed registry carries two loosenings that the append-only workspace stream never recorded (health-telemetry-zero block to warn, graph-outcome-reachable-floor 2438 to 2434), both written by commit 0132ed74b. Filed as pm-h06944 with the full replay diff. Until it is reconciled the assurance registry is frozen for all writes, including no-op re-puts.\n\nSo the batch's state is: three of four legacy codes cleaned to zero in the data, zero of three earned ceilings tightened in the declarations. A regression that re-introduces sentinels, duplicate parent/child spellings or dangling references would still pass CI today. This item should not close until the ceilings are at 0, which makes it dependent on pm-h06944 as well as pm-mfvsng."
  "2026-08-13T09:47:30.966Z","harness:codex","Resume evidence: the new graph audit identifies 31 exact scalar blocked_by plus structured blocks contradictions, reports recorded_nodes=2463 separately from placeholders, and reports informative_edges=12054 separately from 75 redundant and 31 contradictory rows. Workspace assurance replay now agrees with disk after restoring version 167 and reapplying only the pm-jezo-authorized telemetry advisory. Proceeding with the exact blocks-row removals through pm update."
  "2026-08-13T10:07:07.116Z","harness:codex","Changelog evidence: npm latest reports pm-changelog 2026.8.12 and the project installer activated exactly 2026.8.12. The canonical generator added the new graph-ratchet ADR under Unreleased and deterministically repositioned the 41 historical items whose cleanup mutations changed their tracker update chronology. Timestamp-only managed-extension manifest churn was excluded."
  "2026-08-13T10:07:07.965Z","harness:codex","Live cleanup result: removed 31 exact scalar-blocker versus structured-blocks contradictions and 10 additional lower-evidence child-to-prior-milestone ordering rows after fully reading the milestone metadata and history. Current full graph audit: recorded_nodes=2464, informative_edges=12056, redundant_edges=67, ordering_contradiction_edges=0, missing_nodes=0, finding_count=0. The Decision item added after cleanup accounts for the one recorded node and six informative provenance/hierarchy edges above the original cleanup census."
  "2026-08-13T10:42:31.052Z","harness:codex","Final local batch evidence: full graph audit reports finding_count=0, recorded_nodes=2464, informative_edges=12056, redundant_edges=67, ordering_contradiction_edges=0, and missing_nodes=0. Latest pm-changelog 2026.8.12 generated the ADR and deterministic historical chronology. Exact 100/100/100/100 coverage, strict lint, typecheck, contracts, secret/dependency scans, package artifact, npx, 88-command dogfood, and packed Bun/bunx manual acceptance are green."
  "2026-08-13T11:45:45.237Z","harness:codex","Review readiness: local Greptile dispatch on committed head was unavailable with free_reviews_limit_reached. This is a provider limitation, not approval; hosted PR reviewers and exact-head GitHub checks remain required before closure."
